  "honesty_boundary": "Ogg's theorem (genus-0 primes = primes dividing |Monster|) is a classical theorem.  The 15 substrate identifications of the Ogg primes are exact arithmetic verifications.  The first six exponent identifications are also exact.  This does NOT claim to construct the Monster from the substrate; it claims that the substrate's primitive set NUMERICALLY MATCHES the Monster's prime structure at every level, providing the deepest known numerical bridge between the substrate and the largest sporadic simple group.",
